    "user_request_original": "Optimize an 11-layer dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2|SiO2|HfO2. Thickness bounds: 20-150 nm for all layers. Perturbation bounds: ±15% for layers 1, 2, 7, 9; ±10% for layers 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 11. Initialization: hybrid scheme with 50% of candidates seeded from prior best-performing thicknesses (target_score > 0.38) and 50% randomly seeded with ±20% stochastic perturbation from nominal quarter-wave values at 267.5 nm center wavelength. Optimize for maximum transmittance in 255-280 nm band and minimum transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm bands. Use gradient_thickness and differential_evolution_thickness optimizers. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
